Elite Dangerous game data
-------------------------

edrockmaster/domain/engineering/catalogue.json holds game data of Elite Dangerous:
materials and their grades, engineers, blueprints and their ingredients, experimental
effects. This data is the intellectual property and copyright of Frontier Developments plc,
subject to its terms and conditions (https://www.frontierstore.net/terms-and-conditions/).
It is not covered by the plugin's licence.

The file is written by scripts/import_engineering_data.py from community sources, at the
commits it records:

- EDCD/FDevIDs (https://github.com/EDCD/FDevIDs): material.csv, engineers.csv,
  microresources.csv, shipyard.csv.
- EDCD/coriolis-data (https://github.com/EDCD/coriolis-data): modifications/blueprints.json,
  modifications/modules.json, modifications/specials.json.

and from data/odyssey/recipes.toml: the class upgrades and modifications of suits and
weapons, read in the game by the project. Each recipe states how it was known (seen in game,
deduced from rules read in game, or read from public sources, which it names).

and from data/engineers.toml: where each engineer is and how to unlock them, written by the
project in its own words from the game and from public sources, which each entry names.

edrockmaster/domain/trade/commodities.json holds game data of Elite Dangerous too: the
commodities the game trades, their categories and English names, written by
scripts/import_commodities.py from EDCD/FDevIDs' commodity.csv and rare_commodity.csv at the
commit it records. Same owner and terms as above.

